Give the scripts sfall's set_dude_obj: the player plays another critter

As sfall's PartyControl does: the critter takes the player's place (gDude, the inventory's owner, the interface's hands, the critter whose turn it is) with its own name, perks (a party member's), level and addictions, and none of the player's traits, tagged skills, experience or skill points, which come back with control. Experience given meanwhile is the player's once control comes back; scripts asking of the player's own perks and traits are told them; a weapon the critter has no pictures of itself with is not readied. gl_partycontrol uses it with CombatControl Mode 1 or 2.
